{"content":[{"c":["SHAPHAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Son of Azaliah and the father of Ahikam, Elasah, and Gemariah. He and his household favored Josiah’s reforms, supported the prophet Jeremiah, and complied with Babylonian hegemony."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["Shaphan served as the royal secretary to Josiah, king of Judah (640–609 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). He read the Book of the Law to the king after it was found by the high priest Hilkiah in the sanctuary of Jerusalem. Later, Josiah sent him with a small delegation to hear the words of the prophetess Huldah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.22.3-14","r":"2Kgs.22.3-14","rawR":"2Kgs.22.3-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.22.3-14","value":"2Kgs.22.3-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 22:3-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.34.8-28","r":"2Chr.34.8-28","rawR":"2Chr.34.8-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.34.8-28","value":"2Chr.34.8-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 34:8-28"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["Shaphan’s sons were mentioned among the political leaders of Judah during the days of its desolation by Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon (605–586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"). Ahikam assisted with the repair of the sanctuary and protected Jeremiah from the men who sought his death during the reign of King Jehoiakim (609–598 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.22.12","r":"2Kgs.22.12","rawR":"2Kgs.22.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.22.12","value":"2Kgs.22.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 22:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.26.24","r":"Jer.26.24","rawR":"Jer.26.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.26.24","value":"Jer.26.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 26:24"},"). Elasah delivered a message from King Zedekiah of Judah (597–586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") to Nebuchadnezzar in Babylon (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.29.3","r":"Jer.29.3","rawR":"Jer.29.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.29.3","value":"Jer.29.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 29:3"},"). Gemariah was the prince of Judah from whose chamber Baruch read the scroll of Jeremiah to the people (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.10-12","r":"Jer.36.10-12","rawR":"Jer.36.10-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.10-12","value":"Jer.36.10-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:10-12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["Shaphan was the grandfather of Micaiah (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.11-13","r":"Jer.36.11-13","rawR":"Jer.36.11-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.11-13","value":"Jer.36.11-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 36:11-13"},") and Gedaliah. Gedaliah was appointed governor of Judah by Nebuchadnezzar (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.25.22","r":"2Kgs.25.22","rawR":"2Kgs.25.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.25.22","value":"2Kgs.25.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 25:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.40.5-11","r":"Jer.40.5-11","rawR":"Jer.40.5-11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.40.5-11","value":"Jer.40.5-11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 40:5-11"},") and ordered to protect Jeremiah (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.39.14","r":"Jer.39.14","rawR":"Jer.39.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.39.14","value":"Jer.39.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 39:14"},"). Gedaliah was later murdered by a mob led by Ishmael (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.41.2","r":"Jer.41.2","rawR":"Jer.41.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.41.2","value":"Jer.41.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"41:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Father of Jaazaniah and, in Ezekiel’s vision, a leader of idolatrous practices in Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.8.11","r":"Ezek.8.11","rawR":"Ezek.8.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.8.11","value":"Ezek.8.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 8:11"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shaphan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 22:3-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.22.3-14","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.22.3-14","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.22.3-14"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 34:8-28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.34.8-28","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.34.8-28","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.34.8-28"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 22:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.22.12","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.22.12","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.22.12"},{"anchorText":"Jer 26:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.26.24","rawQueryValue":"Jer.26.24","sourceRefExact":"Jer.26.24"},{"anchorText":"Jer 29:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.29.3","rawQueryValue":"Jer.29.3","sourceRefExact":"Jer.29.3"},{"anchorText":"36:10-12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.10-12","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.10-12","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.10-12"},{"anchorText":"Jer 36:11-13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.11-13","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.11-13","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.11-13"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 25:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.25.22","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.25.22","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.25.22"},{"anchorText":"Jer 40:5-11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.40.5-11","rawQueryValue":"Jer.40.5-11","sourceRefExact":"Jer.40.5-11"},{"anchorText":"Jer 39:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.39.14","rawQueryValue":"Jer.39.14","sourceRefExact":"Jer.39.14"},{"anchorText":"41:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.41.2","rawQueryValue":"Jer.41.2","sourceRefExact":"Jer.41.2"},{"anchorText":"Ez 8:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.8.11","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.8.11","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.8.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e7eeebe33e8deaceb409849f4957af06b4746